                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's note: Clearly connected to William Cole merchant who
                            married Thomas Holcroft's daughter Sophia in 1794, he appeared twice
                            with Cole and Gilchrists at Holcroft's in 1797-8, and twice with Mergez
                            (Sophie Holcroft's 2nd husband) in 1820. The most prominent Spirings
                            were Bristol nurserymen and brewers. There was also a John Spiring
                            carpenter of Holborn from 1773 who went bankrupt im 1786. </p>
